    "title": "Warren Buffet invests Billions in the Japanese Yen, $LRE (Lead Real Estate) Benefits Directly",
    "link": "https://www.reddit.com/r/pennystocks/comments/1qh8dfa/warren_buffet_invests_billions_in_the_japanese/",
    "published": "2026-01-19T16:11:13+00:00",
    "summary": "Berkshire is sitting on roughly $350B in cash, and a meaningful portion of it is being invested in the Japanese YEN...(stated in a recent post from Warren Buffett).Whoa right? This is meaningful for $LRE directly.This shift to the YEN anticipates a macro economic shift in the upward direction in Japan, where real estate assets are set to see most of the benefit first.\"LRE owns and operates premium properties in Tokyo, and its flagship ENT TERRACE GINZA PREMIUM just won Luxury Apartments of the Year in Kant\u014d\" (quoted from recent news).So we now look at LRE's low float, no dilution, and upcoming project updates expected, and you\u2019ve got a small-cap that expresses the Buffett/Japan thesis that could see a major upside move.Also, Friday AH, $LRE touched nearly $2. My opinion, news is coming.If all you take from this is that \"Japanese stocks will go up,\" cool. But this weekend LRE is drawing most of the hype. It's trending No1 on Webull as well.submitted by/u/Emotional_Type_3629[link][comments]",
